# {{.Name}} ({{.Type}})

Manage Exoscale [KMS](https://community.exoscale.com/product/security/kms/) External Key Stores.

-> External Key Store is in beta and may change.

An External Key Store connects Exoscale KMS to an XKS proxy that you operate, so that the key material of
[exoscale_kms_key](./kms_key.md) resources can be held in your own key manager. See
[Set Up an External Key Store](https://community.exoscale.com/product/security/kms/how-to/set-up-external-key-store/)
for the proxy requirements.

Corresponding data source: [exoscale_kms_key_store](../data-sources/kms_key_store.md).

~> `proxy.secret_key_wo` is a write-only attribute: it requires Terraform 1.11 or later.

## Example Usage

```terraform
resource "exoscale_kms_key_store" "my_key_store" {
  zone = "ch-gva-2"
  name = "my-key-store"

  proxy = {
    endpoint              = "https://xks.example.com/kms/xks/v1"
    access_key            = var.xks_access_key
    secret_key_wo         = var.xks_secret_key
    secret_key_wo_version = 1
  }

  # KMS keys can only be created in a connected key store.
  connected = true
}

resource "exoscale_kms_key" "my_external_key" {
  zone = "ch-gva-2"
  name = "my-external-key"

  xks = {
    key_store_id    = exoscale_kms_key_store.my_key_store.id
    external_key_id = "<external-key-id>"
  }
}
```

Please refer to the [examples](https://github.com/exoscale/terraform-provider-exoscale/tree/master/examples/)
directory for complete configuration examples.

