## Connection

A key store is created disconnected. While it is disconnected, KMS keys cannot be created in it and its keys
cannot be used for cryptographic operations. Set `connected = true` to have the provider connect it: its keys
can then be used, and Exoscale KMS checks the health of the proxy periodically. Set `connected = false` (the
default) to keep it disconnected, or to suspend every key of the key store at once. If the key store is
connected or disconnected outside of Terraform, the next apply restores the configured value.

Creating, connecting or updating the endpoint or the credentials of a key store runs a health check against the
proxy, and fails if the proxy is unhealthy: a key store is only created if its proxy passes the check.

With `connected = true`, the provider connects the key store right after creating it, and retries for about
30 seconds while the proxy fails the health check. If it still cannot connect, the key store is kept and the
apply ends with a warning instead of an error, so that the key store is not deleted and created again. The key
store then stays disconnected (`status = "disconnected"`), and the next apply tries to connect it again.

The endpoint of a key store can only be changed while it is disconnected. When `proxy.endpoint` changes on a
connected key store, the provider disconnects it, updates it and connects it again in the same apply: its
keys cannot be used for cryptographic operations in the meantime. If the update fails, the provider connects
the key store again with its previous settings.

## Proxy credentials

The secret key is never stored in the Terraform state, so Terraform cannot detect a change of
`secret_key_wo`. To send new credentials, configure them on the proxy first, then change
`secret_key_wo_version` (to any other value) together with `secret_key_wo` and, if needed, `access_key`.
Changing `access_key` alone is rejected, as the API requires both keys together.

## Description

`description` is optional. Once set, it can be changed but not removed: removing it from the configuration
keeps the current description.

## Deletion

A key store is deleted immediately, but only once no KMS key references it. KMS keys keep referencing it
while they are scheduled for deletion (at least 7 days after being destroyed): until then, destroying the key
store fails. Your proxy and external keys are not affected.

## Import

An existing key store may be imported by `<ID>@<zone>`:

```shell
terraform import \
  exoscale_kms_key_store.my_key_store \
  a1b2c3d4-e5f6-4a5b-8c9d-0123456789ab@ch-gva-2
```

The secret key cannot be imported: the first apply after the import sends `secret_key_wo` to the API.
